mode: "100644"
text: "# Signal mines, the matrix & worked examples\n\n## The signal-mine checklist (run weekly, ~15 min)\nComments + DMs since last week clustered (confusion / objections / requests) ✓ · best question from any\nsales/support conversation ✓ · one niche-forum thread with repeated engagement ✓ · competitor top-3 posts\nscanned for pattern + gap ✓ · one People-Also-Ask pull on a pillar ✓ · anything captured mid-week filed ✓.\n\n## The expansion prompt pattern (AI as multiplier, not muse)\n\"Here are [N] real audience signals from this week: [paste clustered comments/questions]. For each theme,\npropose 3 content ideas that would earn saves or shares for [audience], in [brand voice], each mapped to a\npillar and a format.\" — a real signal in, angled multiples out. Never the naked \"10 ideas about X.\"\n\n## The matrix (pillar × format × angle)\n| One idea: \"clients under-price their work\" | Format | Angle |\n|---|---|---|\n| The story | text post | the client who doubled prices and lost nobody |\n| The how-to | carousel | a 4-step repricing walkthrough |\n| The contrarian | text post | \"discounting is lying about your value\" |\n| The proof | quote card / stat | the real before/after number (sourced) |\n| The participation | poll | \"what stops you raising prices?\" (feeds next week's S) |\n\n## The idea-bank card (score each entry)\nIdea · source signal (real, linked) · pillar · segment · format(s) · effort (S/M/L) · demand evidence (none /\nasked once / asked repeatedly) · status (new / probed / scheduled / parked). Weekly review scores; monthly\nrefresh prunes; quarterly audit rebalances pillars.\n\n## The probe ladder (cheap → expensive)\nPoll on the angle → text post of the core claim → carousel → short video → the series/flagship. Each rung's\nreal response (saves/comments/DMs) buys the next rung. Silence = re-angle, not necessarily kill.\n\n## Worked example A — \"Blunt indie founder\" (signal → post)\n\"ran the weekly mine. same question showed up in 4 DMs and a sales call: 'do i need an LLC before my first\nclient?' that's not a content idea, that's a content ORDER. wrote the text post in 20 minutes, it's my best\nperformer this month. my idea system is mostly just listening with a spreadsheet.\" — audience signal, demand\nevidence, fast execution.\n\n## Worked example B — \"Warm bookkeeping studio\" (the matrix stretch)\n\"We worried we'd said everything about tax-season prep. Then we ran one tired topic through the matrix — the\nsame advice became a client story, a five-slide checklist, a gentle myth-bust, and a poll asking what scares\npeople most (which, sweetly, handed us next month's ideas). One small step: pick your most 'finished' topic and\ngive it four new outfits.\" — remix over exhaustion, the loop feeding itself.\n\n## Never\nIdeate on creation day · ask AI for generic idea lists (expansion only, from real signals) · reword a\ncompetitor's post · invent an 'audience question' · manufacture trend urgency · hoard 200 unscored ideas ·\ngreen-light expensive ideas without a probe · fabricate probe results · claim WoopSocial stores ideas.\n"
